Commit:     Fabricio Breve <fbreve@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Oct 20 12:17:53 2026 -0300

    Preserve MD6 handshake state across savestates
    
    Preserve the Mega Drive 6-button controller handshake phase, timeout, TH history, and controller type history independently for both ports.
    
    Freeze controller protocol state during savestate transport so the handshake does not advance while the emulated machine is stopped. Extend the tagged
    savestate payload to version 3 while retaining the existing HCounter and Game Gear state layouts.
    
    Legacy v1/v2 and untagged snapshots remain supported and deterministically normalize MD6 protocol state to its initial phase.
    
    Add directed handshake replay and full DDRAM integration coverage, including the production timeout, both controller ports, legacy formats, stalls, and
    invalid metadata.

